UBI ensures financial stability by providing a consistent income stream, which can reduce stress and improve mental health.
Studies from pilot programs show that UBI can lift people out of poverty without reducing work incentives.
By eliminating the need for unstable jobs, UBI can lead to a more flexible labor market where people can pursue education or entrepreneurship.
UBI simplifies the welfare system, reducing administrative costs and bureaucracy.
It promotes social equity by ensuring everyone has a baseline level of financial security, regardless of their circumstances.